    "\n",
    "#### PCA directions are represented as directions in the **feature space** along which the original data are __highly variable__\n",
    "\n",
    "### __2) Visualization__\n",
    "\n",
    "#### If we have a data __n x p__ where n= number of observations and p = number of features, in EDA, we would like to visualize scatterplot.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### If number of feature is 10 , and we examine 2D scatterplot of the data , we will end up with (p /2) = p * (p-1)/2 => 45 scatterplots!\n",
    "\n",
    "#### if __p is large__, we will not be able to look at all of them, and most of them will not be informative because each one of them contain just a small fraction of total infromation present in the data set.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Considering this case, we would like to find a low-dimensional representation of data that captures as much information as possible."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "15c7fce7",
