    "### Making the covariance matrix S \n",
    "\n",
    "- covariance is the measure of how two variables correlate to eachother\n",
    "\n",
    "- positive score indicates that variables are correlated, meaning that they move in the same direction\n",
    "\n",
    "- my matrix is shape of (5,10). To make covariance matrix i will use the S:\n",
    "\n",
    "### S  = 1 / n - 1 * np.dot(Xc,Xc.T)\n",
    "\n",
    "- 1 / n - 1 because we derive covariance from the sample of population\n",
    "\n",
    "- Xc means that our sample is centered which i will do manually \n",
    "\n",
    "we can not multiply the native shape 5,10 x 5,10 because inner dimmensions need to match\n",
    "\n",
    "if we have 5 features, covariance matrix will be 5x5 matrix:\n"
   ]
