   "source": [
    "A = np.array([[0,1],[-2,-3]]) # 2x2 matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "# A * x = lambda * x = lambda * I * x "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "529f2ac0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### I: Identity matrix, it has ones in the diagnal, other numbers are only zeros\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Identity matrix * any matrix = matrix itself \n",
    "\n",
    "#### 5 * 1 = 5; 1 - represents the I matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "107deb05",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A*x = lambda * I * x\n",
    "\n",
    "A*x - lambda * I * x = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "(A - lambda * I ) * x = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "Parnt in the parenthesis represents matrix M * x = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "-> This notations means that x vector (eigenvector) is in the null  space (kernel) of matrix M \n",
    "\n",
    "-> That implies that this matrix IS NOT invertible \n",
    "\n",
    "-> __Matrix M has determinnat = 0__ !\n",
    "\n",
    "#### det(A - lambda * I ) = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "[[0,1],[-2,-3]] - [[lambda,0],[0,lambda]] = [[-lambda,1],[-2,-3-lambda]]\n",
    "\n",
    "by def. determinant of square matrix (2x2) shape is : ad - bc\n",
    "\n",
    "=> **(-lambda * -3 -lambda) - 1 - (-2) \n",
    "\n",
    "= > **-3_lambda + lambda**2 + 2 = 0**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "=> (lambda + 1) * (lambda + 2) = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "- lambda = -1 and lambda = - 2\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0c304547",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Corresponding eigenvector:\n",
    "\n",
    "A = [[0,1],[-2,-3]]\n",
    "\n",
    "A * (x1,x2) = (-x1,-x2) \n",
    "\n",
    "solving linear equation\n",
    "\n",
    "**[x2 = -x1]**\n",
    "\n",
    "-2x1 - 3x2 = -x2\n",
    "\n",
    "-2x1 + 3x1 = - x2\n",
    "\n",
    "**x2 = -x1** = > x1 = - x2\n"
   ]
